# Paths the PR reviewer does not read (SERV-87).
#
# One extended regex per line, matched against the repository-relative path of
# every changed file. `#` comments and blank lines are ignored.
#
# Per-repo on purpose even though the workflow is shared (SERV-92): which
# artifacts are generated is a fact about this repository. The shared workflow
# reads this from the BASE ref of the PR under review, so widening it in a PR
# does not exempt that PR.
#
# What belongs here is regenerated artifacts, not merely large files. The test
# is: if this file is wrong, is the fix to edit it? For a generated file the
# answer is no — you re-run the generator — so a comment on its diff has nowhere
# to land.

# `make generate` regenerates all three clients from proto/openapi/argosy.yaml
# in one command, so any PR touching a route pays for all of them at once:
# 159KB of Go, 132KB of TypeScript, and an 87-file Dart package. The spec itself
# is NOT excluded — `proto/openapi/argosy.yaml` is hand-authored and is the
# thing worth reviewing when a route changes.
^internal/api/argosy\.gen\.go$
^web/src/api/schema\.ts$
^mobile/argosy/packages/argosy_api/

# The knowledge-graph cache and report. `graphify extract` writes these; 473
# files are committed. The old local workflow carried these as a docs-only
# exception (`docs_skip_extra`), which classified them as documentation; they
# are generated, and this is where generated things go.
^graphify-out/

# Resolved dependency trees. What matters is which dependency moved, and that is
# in pubspec.yaml / package.json, neither of which is excluded.
^mobile/argosy/pubspec\.lock$
^(web/)?bun\.lock(b)?$
